QUESTION 8
As part of the data migration process, the Nautilus DevOps team is actively creating several S3 buckets on AWS. They plan to utilize both private and public S3 buckets to store the relevant data. Given the ongoing migration of other infrastructure to AWS, it is logical to consolidate data storage within the AWS environment as well.

Create a public S3 bucket named xfusion-s3-937853010-t4q2 using Terraform.

Ensure the bucket is accessible publicly once created by setting the proper ACL.

The Terraform working directory is /home/bob/terraform/t4q2. Create the main.tf file (do not create a different .tf file) to accomplish this task.

Notes:

Create the resources only in the us-east-1 region.
Right-click under the EXPLORER section in VS Code and select Open in Integrated Terminal to launch the terminal.
The name of the S3 bucket should be based on xfusion-s3-937853010-t4q2.
You can use the ACL settings to ensure the bucket is publicly accessible.

'xfusion-s3-937853010-t4q2' Public S3 bucket was created using 'Terraform'?

SOLUTION
Here is the main.tf for the /home/bob/terraform/t4q2 working directory to create the public S3 bucket.

📄 /home/bob/terraform/t4q2/main.tf
hcl
# Create the S3 bucket
resource "aws_s3_bucket" "xfusion_bucket" {
  bucket = "xfusion-s3-937853010-t4q2"

  tags = {
    Name = "xfusion-s3-937853010-t4q2"
  }
}

# Set ownership controls so ACLs can be applied
resource "aws_s3_bucket_ownership_controls" "xfusion_bucket_ownership" {
  bucket = aws_s3_bucket.xfusion_bucket.id

  rule {
    object_ownership = "BucketOwnerPreferred"
  }
}

# Disable the public access block that AWS applies by default
resource "aws_s3_bucket_public_access_block" "xfusion_bucket_public_access" {
  bucket = aws_s3_bucket.xfusion_bucket.id

  block_public_acls       = false
  block_public_policy     = false
  ignore_public_acls      = false
  restrict_public_buckets = false
}

# Apply the public-read ACL to make the bucket publicly accessible
resource "aws_s3_bucket_acl" "xfusion_bucket_acl" {
  depends_on = [
    aws_s3_bucket_ownership_controls.xfusion_bucket_ownership,
    aws_s3_bucket_public_access_block.xfusion_bucket_public_access,
  ]

  bucket = aws_s3_bucket.xfusion_bucket.id
  acl    = "public-read"
}
💡 Key Details
Bucket Name: Exactly xfusion-s3-937853010-t4q2 as required.

aws_s3_bucket_ownership_controls: Sets object_ownership to BucketOwnerPreferred, which is required for ACLs to take effect.

aws_s3_bucket_public_access_block: All four flags set to false to disable AWS's default public access restrictions.

aws_s3_bucket_acl: Applies the public-read canned ACL. The depends_on ensures the ownership controls and public access block are configured first, preventing a race condition.

Region: Handled by provider.tf in the t4q2/ directory (us-east-1).

⚠️ Ensure provider.tf Exists in t4q2/
Terraform only reads .tf files from the current working directory. Copy the provider configuration:

bash
cp /home/bob/terraform/provider.tf /home/bob/terraform/t4q2/
🚀 Execution Steps
bash
cd /home/bob/terraform/t4q2
